# Windows entry points must keep CRLF line endings in the working tree on every
# platform. cmd.exe tolerates LF in most cases but not all -- a `goto :label`
# whose line ends in a bare LF has been observed to fail -- and PowerShell's
# here-strings and `param()` block are likewise sensitive. tests/test_launcher.py
# asserts CRLF on these files, so without this a clone on Linux (which is what CI
# runs) would check them out normalized and fail the assertion.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Everything else: normalize to LF in the repository, let git decide the working
# tree. This is git's default behaviour, stated explicitly so a future
# core.autocrlf setting on a contributor's machine cannot change it.
* text=auto eol=lf
